BEHAVIOR extract-body

DESCRIPTION
  Finds the CR LF CR LF header/body separator in an HTTP request and copies the
  body that follows into body, with its length. Uses find to locate the
  separator (at index), then copies recv_len - (index + 4) bytes starting just
  after it. Assumes a well-formed request whose separator is present within
  recv_len bytes.

CONTRACT
  INPUT request bytes 65536
  INPUT recv_len int 8
  OUTPUT body bytes 65536
  OUTPUT body_len int 8
  REQUIRES crlf-needle@3190a1f5 find@7f2c5e1c add-int@506d7b8d sub-int@506d7b8d copy@05c62b49
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH 52d1aba6

COMPOSITION
  n = CALL crlf-needle
  sep = CALL find request n.needle
  start = CALL add-int sep.index 4
  bl = CALL sub-int recv_len start.result
  SET body_len bl.result
  cb = CALL copy request start.result body 0 bl.result
  DISCARD cb.bytes_copied
END
